Upstream local_sensing latches the first global map and ignores every later one
(`if (has_global_map) return;`).  That makes the rendered local cloud a function
of the very first map message only, so a deliberate obstacle published later can
never reach the planners.

M2 needs a deterministic obstacle that the planners actually see, so the map is
refreshed instead of latched: each message replaces the voxelised map and the
k-d tree.  The upstream file is not modified in the repository; this patch is
applied at image build time and is recorded here.

--- a/src/uav_simulator/local_sensing/src/pointcloud_render_node.cpp
+++ b/src/uav_simulator/local_sensing/src/pointcloud_render_node.cpp
@@ -79,9 +79,7 @@
 
 void rcvGlobalPointCloudCallBack(
     const sensor_msgs::PointCloud2& pointcloud_map) {
-  if (has_global_map) return;
-
-  ROS_WARN("Global Pointcloud received..");
+  ROS_WARN_ONCE("Global Pointcloud received; map updates are accepted.");
 
   pcl::PointCloud<pcl::PointXYZ> cloud_input;
   pcl::fromROSMsg(pointcloud_map, cloud_input);
